% ============================================================================
%  PP2.till — minimal Paragon Pioneers 2 core, on calc's till (Timed ILL).
%
%  THE MODEL (calc TODO_0265, the locked design):
%    * every linear fact carries an ABSOLUTE availability stamp  A@t ;  two
%      tokens of the same kind at different stamps are distinct cohorts.
%    * a rule  In -o { Out }@d  fires ASAP at its activation
%      a = max(stamps of consumed inputs);  it consumes at a and produces at
%      a+d — between a and a+d the job is IN FLIGHT.  That gap is {_}@d, the
%      graded lax monad (duration as an effect grade).
%    * a  building * ... -o { building * ... }@d  pair (or the $ sugar) is a
%      SINGLE-SERVER machine: the token is absent (busy) from a to a+d.
%    * there is NO clock in the state.  settle(state, T) runs the schedule to
%      horizon T;  the horizon is an observation cursor, not a resource
%      (settle(settle(S,T1),T2) = settle(S,T2) — composability, E5).
%    * count grades:  !_k A  = k-token parcel (spread across cohorts,
%      oldest-first);  !_W A  binds ALL copies, W = the total at firing time
%      (D4 revised: binding discipline decides cohort discipline — the
%      stamped forms !_k A@T / !_W A@T stay cohort-locked).  Counts
%      are naturals (bin);  stamps/delays are exact rationals.  Arithmetic is
%      the bin family (!mul, !div, !min, …) — backward clauses with FFI fast
%      paths (FFI is optimization, theory is semantics).
%    * windows:  after E / before E  bound a rule's activation (E may use
%      matched stamps: spoilage below).  read P = instantaneous measurement.
%    * POSSESSED RULES (Phase 6c): a loli FACT in the state is a rule you
%      own — one-shot by linearity, fireable from its own stamp onward, its
%      delay read from the stored {..}@d.  The menus below are made of them.
%    * conflicts (same cohort wanted by two equal-activation matches) resolve
%      by a seeded stateless PRF — settle replays bit-identically per seed;
%      settleExplore branches on genuine conflicts only.
%
%  THE PLAYER: the game OFFERS, the player COLLAPSES.  A menu is a standing
%  persistent external choice whose alternatives ARE the costed rules —
%  price and product visible in the menu's very type.  A click is a proof
%  step:  CUT (default) fires the possessed rule at the decision time or is
%  refused outright (the PP2 button you can't click);  PLAN residuates it
%  into the context as a queued order.  See section 5.
%
%  COMBAT is combat.till's single `duel` rule run to quiescence: sampled
%  under settle (seeded), exact distribution under settleExplore.
%
%  Run the gates:   npm run test:till   (from calc)
% ============================================================================

#import(../prelude/rat.ill)
#import(combat.till)

% ======================= 0. TOKENS (atomic propositions) ====================
% Every resource and building is DECLARED, CLF/Celf-style: `wood: type.`
% introduces the atomic proposition wood — possessing it is the linear fact.
% (An arity-n token is a type family: red: (u: utype) -> type, combat.till.)
% Storable goods form a CLASSIFIER (refinement sort, TODO_0011 rung 1):
% members stay ordinary atomic propositions; the warehouse schema (3b)
% expands once per member.  food is deliberately NOT storable — the spoil
% window already bounds it;  space is build capacity, not a warehouse good.
storable: sort.
wood: storable.
stone: storable.
plank: storable.
tool: storable.
charcoal: storable.
bread: storable.
iron_ore: storable.
iron: storable.
food: type.
space: type.

lumberjack: type.
quarry: type.
sawmill: type.
smith: type.
farm: type.
bakery: type.
kiln: type.
mine: type.
smelter: type.
barracks: type.

bot: type.

% ======================= 1. PRODUCTION (timed single servers) ===============
% Raw producers tap the environment and yield one good per cycle; recipes
% consume inputs.  The cycle time is the only coupling to time — there is no
% per-turn `ready` token, no `arm`, no `new_turn`.

lumberjack: $lumberjack -o { wood  }@(2/5).
quarry:     $quarry     -o { stone }@(3/10).
farm:       $farm       -o { food  }@6.

sawmill: $sawmill * wood          -o { plank }@(1/2).
smith:   $smith   * plank * stone -o { tool  }@(3/10).

% Fixed-grade recipe: !_2 splits two food off the oldest cohort.
bakery: $bakery * !_2 food -o { bread }@8.

% Mine: raw iron ore from the mountain seam.
mine:    $mine -o { iron_ore }@(3/10).

% Smelter: converts iron ore + charcoal into refined iron.
smelter: $smelter * iron_ore * charcoal -o { iron }@5.

% ======================= 2. THE KILN (batch multiplication) =================
% A batch furnace, not a single-unit server: one firing chars ALL wood on
% hand — duration per batch, yield multiplicative (each log splits into
% pieces): W logs -> floor(3W/2) charcoal, capped by the chamber (12); an
% overloaded kiln burns the surplus to ash.  W binds the total wood count
% at firing time (D4 revised whole-bind, spread across cohorts).
kiln:
  $kiln
  * !_W wood
  * !mul W 3 T          % T = 3W
  * !div T 2 A          % A = floor(3W/2)
  * !min A 12 Y         % Y = min(A, 12) — chamber cap
  -o { !_Y charcoal }@10.

% ======================= 3. SPOILAGE (windows) ==============================
% Food keeps 20 time units; the whole cohort rots in one event.  Consumers
% win races by activation order (eat at a < Q+20 beats spoil), not by luck.
spoil: !_W food@Q * after (Q + 20) -o { I }.

% ======================= 3b. WAREHOUSE (stock caps) =========================
% Every storable good is capped at 200.  The overflow rule burns one net
% unit per fire down to the cap — the kiln's ash precedent, warehouse-wide.
% One schema, one rule per member at load.  The 201-take IS the guard (a
% counted take needs 201 on hand — no arithmetic premise), so gate-sized
% stocks never see it;  the kept 200 re-emit as ONE cohort — storable
% stamps are unobserved (only food spoils), coalesce merges them anyway.
%
% Deliberately NOT `!_W g * !lt 200 W`: a whole-bind includes the in-flight
% cohort a producer just scheduled, so its activation chases every arrival
% and a deterministic chooser can starve the trim FOREVER (the PRF chooser
% merely hides it).  The counted take spreads oldest-first — its activation
% pins to the 201st-oldest cohort and later arrivals leave it alone:
% starvation-free under ANY chooser.  Bounded stocks are what let
% acceleration certify a full warehouse as a zero-net-growth orbit
% (TODO_0278 item 4, content side).
overflow: (g: storable) !_201 g -o { !_200 g }.

% ======================= 4. SPACE (scarce, graded) ==========================
% Free space is one count-graded atom !_n space; scarcity is a theorem (no
% build fires without the grade).  Space is FUNGIBLE: reclaimed parcels
% arrive as separate cohorts and a counted take !_k splits from ONE cohort
% only (D4) — so cohorts merge eagerly, stamped at the max (k space exists
% as a unit once its last parcel arrived).  Cross-cohort totals WITHOUT
% merging = aggregation, deferred to the fluid ladder (todo 0265 res. iii).
merge_space: !_W space * !_V space * !plus W V T -o { !_T space }.

% ======================= 4b. DISPLAY GROUPING (presentation hints) ===========
%#display resource: wood stone food plank tool charcoal bread iron_ore iron space
%#display building: lumberjack quarry sawmill smith farm bakery kiln mine smelter barracks
%#display army: red blue

% ======================= 5. THE PLAYER: MENUS OF COSTED RULES ===============
% There are no act tokens and no build_* rules: a menu ALTERNATIVE IS the
% rule it triggers — a possessed loli, price on the left, product on the
% right, construction time on the monad.  The standing build menu (put it
% in the initial state; the gates and the shell do):
%
%   !( (!_5 space -o { farm }@20)
%    & (!_3 space -o { barracks * ARMY_MENU }@15)
%    & (!_4 space -o { kiln }@25)
%    & (I -o { !_2 blue(rock) * !_2 blue(paper) * !_2 blue(sci) }) )
%
% Reading it:
%   * !(A & B) ≅ !A ⊗ !B (Seely): a persistent menu is an unlimited supply
%     of its alternatives; projection never consumes it.  A LINEAR menu is
%     a one-shot/revocable offer (rules and windows can take it back).
%   * building the barracks UNLOCKS the army menu — the persistent training
%     menu (three costed recruit rules) appears with the barracks
%     (visibility as game logic);  training is a single-server recipe
%     (barracks consumed, returned at +12).
%   * the attack alternative is a costless rule (I -o …): projecting it
%     seeds the garrison and the duel runs to quiescence.
%   * CUT click (default): choose() refuses unless the rule fires at the
%     decision time — greying (menuStatus) and enforcement are the same
%     relation by construction.  PLAN click ({plan: true}): the possessed
%     rule waits in the context and fires when its cost exists — a queued
%     order (see expect_plan_waits).
%
% `bot` is the optional self-playing policy — the CONTRAST to the menu:
% woplus is internal choice (the game's own chance), so the bot's draw is
% the engine's to make.  It draws ORDERS (possessed rules), which then fire
% when affordable.  Include a `bot` token to demo an autonomous run.
bot:
  $bot
  -o { woplus (1/3) (!_5 space -o { farm }@20)
       (woplus (1/2) (barracks * food * !_2 plank -o { barracks * red(rock) }@12)
                     (I -o { !_2 blue(rock) * !_2 blue(paper) * !_2 blue(sci) })) }@5.

% ======================= 6. DISPLAY GROUPING (presentation, NOT logic) ======
% The shell groups its state view by these rows.  This is deliberately a
% COMMENT directive: classifying atomic propositions in-logic would need
% quantification over propositions (kind: (x: type) -> ...), which the
% theory does not support — the sort checker now REJECTS it.  When the
% classifier-sort extension lands (ltype <: type, todo 0265 / 6b), this
% moves back into the logic as declarations.
%#display resource: wood stone food plank tool charcoal bread space
%#display building: lumberjack quarry sawmill smith farm bakery kiln barracks
%#display army: red blue

% ======================= 7. COMBAT ==========================================
% Your red(U) soldiers duel the sector garrison to quiescence (combat.till).
% Each casualty emits fell*(Type); territory is the residue of attrition.
reclaim: fellb(V) -o { space }.   % garrison unit down -> +1 space reclaimed
losses:  fellr(U) -o { I }.       % your casualty: gone (affine discard)

% ======================= 8. GATES ===========================================
% Phase 6 acceptance (calc TODO_0265): the 10/10/10 scenario on the REAL PP2
% calculus.  Hand-computed schedule (= time.mjs oracle): sawmill jobs at 0,
% 1/2, 1;  smith jobs at 0, 3/10, 3/5, 9/10 (FIFO takes plank@0).
#expect_gate_10_10_10 (settle: 1, exact: true)
  sawmill * smith * !_10 wood * !_10 plank * !_10 stone
  =>
  !_7 wood@0 * !_6 plank@0 * plank@(1/2) * plank@1 * plank@(3/2)
  * !_6 stone@0 * tool@(3/10) * tool@(3/5) * tool@(9/10) * tool@(6/5)
  * sawmill@(3/2) * smith@(6/5) .

#expect_not_five_tools (settle: 1)
  sawmill * smith * !_10 wood * !_10 plank * !_10 stone
  =>
  !_5 tool .

#expect_drained (settle: 100)
  sawmill * smith * !_10 wood * !_10 plank * !_10 stone
  =>
  !_10 tool * !_10 plank * sawmill * smith .

% --- kiln: batch multiplication, chamber cap, cohort separation -------------
#expect_kiln_batch (settle: 20, exact: true)
  kiln * !_3 wood
  =>
  !_4 charcoal@10 * kiln@10 .           % floor(4.5) = 4

#expect_kiln_cap (settle: 20, exact: true)
  kiln * !_10 wood
  =>
  !_12 charcoal@10 * kiln@10 .          % min(15, 12) — surplus burned

#expect_kiln_cohorts (settle: 30, exact: true)
  kiln * !_3 wood * !_5 wood@1
  =>
  !_12 charcoal@11 * kiln@11 .   % D4 revised: unstamped !_W spreads across
                                 % cohorts (W = 8 total, activation = newest
                                 % taken stamp 1); 3W/2 = 12 = chamber cap

% --- spoilage: consumers beat the window; leftovers rot as one cohort -------
#expect_bakery_beats_spoil (settle: 30, exact: true)
  bakery * !_3 food
  =>
  bread@8 * bakery@8 .                  % 2 food baked at 0; 1 rots at 20

#expect_not_food_survives (settle: 30)
  bakery * !_3 food
  =>
  food .

% --- warehouse: overflow burns the surplus down to the cap ------------------
#expect_overflow (settle: 1, exact: true)
  !_250 wood
  =>
  !_200 wood@0 .

#expect_at_cap_inert (settle: 1, exact: true)
  !_200 wood
  =>
  !_200 wood@0 .

% --- possessed build orders -------------------------------------------------
% a projected build order fires at once when affordable; the farm then cycles
#expect_build (settle: 21, exact: true)
  (!_5 space -o { farm }@20) * !_8 space
  =>
  !_3 space@0 * farm@26 * food@26 .

% training: single-server recipe as a possessed rule
#expect_recruit (settle: 12, exact: true)
  (barracks * food * !_2 plank -o { barracks * red(rock) }@12)
  * barracks * food * !_2 plank
  =>
  red(rock)@12 * barracks@12 .

% a PLAN order waits: space reclaimed at 4 (three peasants fall) merges with
% the stock, completes the 5 needed, and the farm goes up
#expect_plan_waits (settle: 23, exact: true)
  (!_5 space -o { farm }@20) * !_2 space * red(hero) * !_3 blue(peasant)@4
  =>
  red(hero)@4 * farm@24 .

% --- menus: standing offers are inert; barracks unlocks the army menu -------
#expect_standing_inert (settle: 10, exact: true)
  !( (!_5 space -o { farm }@20)
   & (!_4 space -o { kiln }@25)
   & (I -o { !_2 blue(rock) * !_2 blue(paper) * !_2 blue(sci) }) )
  * wood
  =>
  !( (!_5 space -o { farm }@20)
   & (!_4 space -o { kiln }@25)
   & (I -o { !_2 blue(rock) * !_2 blue(paper) * !_2 blue(sci) }) )
  * wood@0 .

#expect_army_menu_unlocked (settle: 15, exact: true)
  (!_3 space -o { barracks
     * !( (barracks * food * !_2 plank -o { barracks * red(rock) }@12)
        & (barracks * food * !_2 plank -o { barracks * red(paper) }@12)
        & (barracks * food * !_2 plank -o { barracks * red(sci) }@12) ) }@15)
  * !_3 space
  =>
  !( (barracks * food * !_2 plank -o { barracks * red(rock) }@12)
   & (barracks * food * !_2 plank -o { barracks * red(paper) }@12)
   & (barracks * food * !_2 plank -o { barracks * red(sci) }@12) )
  * barracks@15 .

% --- combat (deterministic edges; the weighted distribution is pinned
%     against the absorbing-chain DP in calc's engine suite) ----------------
#expect_hero_conquers (settle: 0, exact: true)
  red(hero) * !_2 blue(peasant)
  =>
  red(hero)@0 * !_2 space@0 .           % 2 duels, 2 reclaims, zero time

#expect_not_peasant_survives (settle: 0)
  red(hero) * !_2 blue(peasant)
  =>
  blue(peasant) .

#expect_peasant_falls (settle: 0, exact: true)
  red(peasant) * blue(hero)
  =>
  blue(hero)@0 .                        % the 1-Q branch, deterministically

% the attack order is a costless possessed rule: garrison seeded, swept
#expect_assault (settle: 0, exact: true)
  (I -o { !_2 blue(rock) * !_2 blue(paper) * !_2 blue(sci) }) * !_6 red(hero)
  =>
  !_6 red(hero)@0 * !_6 space@0 .

% --- a played session: the residue of two projections, one settle ----------
% t=0 CUT build farm; t=25 CUT train rock (the order carries its stamp).
% farm up at 20, cycles at 20, 26, 32, 38; soldier ready at 37.  All food
% cohorts still fresh at 40 (spoil at stamp+20).
#expect_session (settle: 40, exact: true)
  (!_5 space -o { farm }@20) * !_8 space * barracks
  * (barracks * food * !_2 plank -o { barracks * red(rock) }@12)@25
  * food@25 * !_2 plank@25
  =>
  !_3 space@0 * red(rock)@37 * barracks@37
  * farm@44 * food@26 * food@32 * food@38 * food@44 .

% --- the live shell's start state (from calc:  npm run shell:till --
%     calculus/till/game/PP2.till --init expect_shell_start) -----------------
#expect_shell_start (settle: 0)
  !( (!_5 space -o { farm }@20)
   & (!_3 space -o { barracks
        * !( (barracks * food * !_2 plank -o { barracks * red(rock) }@12)
           & (barracks * food * !_2 plank -o { barracks * red(paper) }@12)
           & (barracks * food * !_2 plank -o { barracks * red(sci) }@12) ) }@15)
   & (!_4 space -o { kiln }@25)
   & (!_4 space -o { mine }@18)
   & (!_5 space -o { smelter }@22)
   & (I -o { !_2 blue(rock) * !_2 blue(paper) * !_2 blue(sci) }) )
  * lumberjack * quarry * sawmill * smith * mine
  * !_6 space * !_6 wood * !_4 stone * !_4 plank * !_3 food * !_2 iron_ore * red(hero)
  =>
  !_4 space .
